{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"m01","type":"text","text":"## Module 01 — Specification Analysis 🟡\n**Done:** 4-phase pipeline (~1,950 LOC) — dynamic extractor with recovery pass, LTLf synthesis, multi-round mutation self-healing + adversarial tier, and **Phase 4 PBCTS** (pure-Python LTLf progression → trace synthesis, BDA alignment, IDCD convergence, SCSL self-correction → Formal Reliability Certificate v2.0).\n**Pivot:** SPOT/HOA Phase 4 + process-mining Phase 5 were deleted after one day; SPOT gone from code (still built in Dockerfile — dead weight).\n**Alarming:** still zero tests; **`main.py` imports the deleted `automata_lifter` → spec-engine crashes on startup**.","x":-760,"y":-480,"width":700,"height":230,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"m02","type":"text","text":"## Module 02 — Verified IR Extraction 🟢 (most mature)\n~3,000 LOC · tests + serious eval harness. **Unchanged this cycle** — thesis Chapter 5 draft (§5.1–5.8) + figures under `docs/thesis/`.\n**Measured:** genuine-bug detection 0.9952 (n=210) · false-alarm 0.0588 (n=51) · WIR structural F1 1.0 · natural-bug detection 1.0 strict / 0.9329 task_only.\n**Eval assets:** FLOW-BENCH (101 workflows, vendored at repo root), 427 mutants, Youden's J calibration + CIs, natural-bug corpus from 3 LLM families.\n**Honest limits:** V2 ≈ no contribution on corpus (certificate is V1-driven); equivalent-mutant specificity 0.1111; numeric-boundary bugs are a known blind spot.\n**Integration:** consumes M01's `task_patterns` (`module_02_input.json`) — the one wired cross-module handoff.","x":0,"y":-480,"width":700,"height":230,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"m03","type":"text","text":"## Module 03 — Equivalence Engine 🟡 (documented method now executable)\n**Done:** pure-Python pipeline (37 tests) intact; C++/SPOT engine now covers **ALL phases A–D** — lifter.cpp 1,262 LOC, including `check_compliance`: SPOT ¬φ → Büchi → product → emptiness + counterexample trace. **113 tests** total (76 C++-side, skipif no .so); `process_wir_batch()` runs the full A→D chain.\n**Pending:** Module 01 ingestion — the only caller uses a hardcoded `'G(\"approved\")'` placeholder; LTLf→LTL bridge missing. `main.py` still a stale milestone demo.","x":-760,"y":-210,"width":700,"height":240,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"m04","type":"text","text":"## Module 04 — Verification Portal 🟡\n565-line Streamlit app, 4 pages; talks to Modules 01/02 over HTTP fine. **Unchanged.**\n**Broken by construction:** the equivalence page does an in-process `import vibecheck_lifter` inside the UI container, which has no SPOT — cannot work under docker-compose. (Committed Linux .so since removed from git; still dead on macOS without a local build.)\nNo tests. `networkx` in requirements but unused. Explicitly disclaims research novelty (integration layer).","x":0,"y":-210,"width":700,"height":240,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"strengths","type":"text","text":"## Strengths ✅\n- Sound dual-track independence (no circular verification)\n- Exceptional epistemic discipline: measured fact vs design intent labeled everywhere; limitations stated with costs attached\n- Real measured evaluation with CIs + archived pre-fix report audit trail\n- Module 02 is legitimately good engineering (PEP 669 tracer, parity tests, timeouts)\n- Schema-first WIR contract between modules\n- C++/SPOT equivalence core now complete (Phases A–D) and tested — the documented method is executable","x":-760,"y":70,"width":700,"height":240,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"gaps","type":"text","text":"## Gaps / risks ⚠️\n- E2E spec↔code still not wired: M01 exports LTLf strings, M03 `check_compliance` accepts SPOT LTL — **no ingestion code, no LTLf→LTL bridge**\n- **M01 startup bug** (imports deleted `automata_lifter`) — spec-engine Docker service broken\n- M01 zero tests (3rd cycle running); no CI (`.github/` = CODEOWNERS only)\n- Two M03 Phase D flavors (Python reachability vs C++ SPOT), no canonical declared\n- `docs/` tree removed from the repo (develop @ 05fae60) — survives only in the local vault + git history; V2 layer dead weight on the eval corpus","x":0,"y":70,"width":700,"height":240,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"next","type":"text","text":"**Recommended priorities:** 1) fix M01 `main.py` import (service is down) 2) build the LTLf→LTL bridge + feed `module_03_input.json` into `process_wir_batch` (e2e at last) 3) restore M01 tests + add CI 4) drop SPOT from M01 Dockerfile (dead weight since PBCTS).","x":-760,"y":350,"width":1460,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# VibeCheck — Whole-Project Status\nSnapshot: 2026-07-28 (main @ 7089711) · FYP Group Epsilon, University of Moratuwa","x":-760,"y":-900,"width":1460,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"verdict","type":"text","text":"## Overall verdict\n**The headline end-to-end claim is mechanically possible for the first time — but still not wired.** M01 produces an LTLf property suite (+ PBCTS reliability certificate) and M03's C++ engine runs real SPOT model checking with counterexamples; nothing connects them yet (hardcoded placeholder property, no LTLf→LTL bridge).\n**What runs today:** WIR extraction + 3-layer certificate (M02, evidence-backed), code-vs-code behavioral equivalence + LTL compliance checking (M03, 113 tests), and M01's 4-phase PBCTS pipeline. **Red flags:** M01 zero tests and a startup crash in its FastAPI app; two architectural pivots in two days.","x":-760,"y":-740,"width":1460,"height":160,"color":"3"}
	],
